# Agent tooling and its worktrees. This repo is PUBLIC, so anything landing here lands
# publicly. Nothing was exposed -- .claude/ currently holds only a registered git worktree,
# which git will not descend into -- but the directory itself was unignored, so any ordinary
# file it later gained (settings, agents, commands) would have committed cleanly with nothing
# to stop it. The sibling burnsidesteps repo had the same gap and fixed it the same day.
.claude/
